AMOUNT
delta = abs(assessment - market_price)
amount = int(delta * scale * conviction)

So basically, if you want to gain a larger share in the market, 
you have to make the assessment level either much higher or much lower than the current market probability.
Which is currently: {market_current_probability}

You also must use a higher conviction level, since that acts as a filter for your bet size.

If your betting strategy is agressive, then you have to set your assessement level to deviate from the market price 
toward the direction you believe the market will end up on the market resolution datetime, which is {resolution_datetime}.

However if your betting strategy is more conservative, or you're just not sure, then your bets should be low.

You should also keep an eye on your balance, and match that to your betting strategy. Earlier more accurate predictions get rewarded with higher shares.
However if you are being more conservative, you may want to conserve your balance until close to the resolution time to make a larger bet.

